.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 

.SS "template<class T>
.br
class cbor::static_dictionary< T >"Writes and reads a message of \fRT\fP without its description: the description is a static dictionary (draft-ietf-cbor-packed-19, section 3)\&. 

Each form has the name, the arguments and the result of the form of cbor::schema\&. \fR\fBencode\fP\fP writes the message without cbor::schema::description(), and the read forms read such a message\&. Use it to store the description once and the data of each key in another place, for example in two named databases of LMDB\&. The data form is one well-formed CBOR item: tag 113 on the table without the description and the rump\&. The count of the table counts only the entries that it holds\&. The references keep the indices of the message with the description, so only \fR\fBcbor::static_dictionary\fP<T>\fP reads the data form\&. A generic decoder of Packed CBOR does not\&. The size of the data form plus the size of \fRdescription()\fP is the size of the message\&. The other errors are the errors of cbor::schema::adopt(), cbor::schema::at_path() and cbor::schema::decode()\&.

.PP
